ISSUE:
`ObjectMapper.valueToTree()` with `byte[]` does not produce `BinaryNode`

### Search before asking

- [x] I searched in the [issues](https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-databind/issues) and found nothing similar.

### Describe the bug

Json node generated from the same object instance are not equal.
In v2 [JsonNodeDeserializer._fromEmbedded](https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-databind/blob/2.15/src/main/java/com/fasterxml/jackson/databind/deser/std/JsonNodeDeserializer.java#L826) instantiate a BinaryNode.
In v3 [TreeBuildingGenerator.writeBinary](https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-databind/blob/3.x/src/main/java/tools/jackson/databind/node/TreeBuildingGenerator.java#L496) instantiate a POJONode.

Only BinaryNode use Arrays.equals to compare arrays.

### Version Information

3.2.0

### Reproduction

```java
package test;

import static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.assertEquals;

import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;

public class JacksonBinaryTest {

    byte[] byteArray = new byte[0];

    @Test
    void jacksonV2() {
        var mapper = com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.json.JsonMapper.builder().build();
        var jRecord1 = mapper.valueToTree(byteArray);
        var jRecord2 = mapper.valueToTree(byteArray);
        assertEquals(jRecord1, jRecord2);
    }

    @Test
    void jacksonV3() {
        var mapper = tools.jackson.databind.json.JsonMapper.builder().build();
        var jRecord1 = mapper.valueToTree(byteArray);
        var jRecord2 = mapper.valueToTree(byteArray);
        assertEquals(jRecord1, jRecord2); // Failed
    }
}
```

